jala (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
    - Add --calendar=auto|jalali|gregorian for -c and -d.
    - Replace the 33-year leap-year cycle with the jalaali-js
      algorithm (Borkowski 1996), matching the official Iranian
      calendar for the modern era.
    - Enforce MAX_YEAR = 3177, the upper bound of the era table.
    - Fix the version string in main.cpp, which still reported
      1.2.0 after the 1.3.0 release.

 -- Mahdi Moradi <Soshianth@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0330

jala (1.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
    - Remove the Boost.Date_Time dependency. The Gregorian calendar
      layer is now implemented locally in src/gregorian.{hpp,cpp}
      using the Fliegel-Van Flandern JDN formulas.
    - Secularize holiday descriptions at build time via
      scripts/neutralize_overrides.py and data/manual_overrides.json.
    - Keep the 33-year Jalali leap-year cycle from 1.2.0.
    - Move src/holidays_data.hpp and data/overrides.json out of
      version control; they are now generated by the build.
    - Add python3 to Build-Depends, needed by the generator scripts.
    - Bump Standards-Version to 4.7.2.

 -- Mahdi Moradi <Soshianth@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 15:40:46 +0330

jala (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
    - Add --color=always|never|auto.
    - Use the 33-year cycle consistently for all conversions.
    - Strict input validation in parse_date().
    - Use wcwidth() for accurate terminal column widths.
    - Fix --no-bidi with -p (weekday header order).
    - Catch Boost exceptions and report clean errors.
    - Preserve Debian hardening flags in debian/rules.
    - Split debian/copyright for the holiday dataset.
    - Remove the obsolete monolithic jala.cpp.

 -- Mahdi Moradi <Soshianth@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0330

jala (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
    - Add -E/--events to list all events.
    - Add -H/--no-holidays.
    - Add -B/--no-bidi.
    - Use hasan-ahani/shamsi-holidays (MIT) as data source.

